ftuser - first-time user introduction to ZEUS
files - basic file handling commands
editor - text editor; you must know about files first
morefiles - more on file manipulations and other useful stuff
macros - "-ms" macros for memos & papers; you must know editor
eqn - typing mathematics; you must know editor
C - writing programs in the C language; you must know editor

This is probably the best order, but after you have taken
the "files" course and know the basics of "editor", you can
try anything you like.

You can always leave learn by typing:  bye (RETURN)
You can stop learn from typing by pressing (RUB), which is an
interrupt, or (BREAK). If learn won't accept your answer and
you know you're right, type in the answer:  no (RETURN)
when it asks whether you want to try the lesson again.
